    "result_text": "Done. The membership level rules are now a points system, and the test suite is green.\n\n## What changed\n\n**Points formula** (start at 0):\n- `+2` email present \u00b7 `+1` `namesakeCount == 0` \u00b7 `+2` household of 3+ \u00b7 `+3` tenure > 365 days\n\n**Points \u2192 level:** 1 (0\u20131) \u00b7 2 (2\u20133) \u00b7 3 (4\u20135) \u00b7 4 (6+). Both `membershipPoints` and `membershipLevel` are returned.\n\n**Files:**\n- `src/main/resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` field (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it) and updated `membershipLevel` (description + `maximum: 4`).\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 new `membershipPoints(owner)` implementing the additive formula; `membershipLevel(owner)` now maps points to a band; both wired via `@Mapping` expressions.\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `@Transient householdSize` (defaults to 1; not persisted) feeding the household factor.\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 added a `householdSize(owner)` helper that counts owners sharing the `householdId` (reusing the existing `countOwners`), and populates it on the create and read decoration paths.\n\nThe household factor needed a repository count that the field-only mapper can't do, so I kept the point math in the mapper (one place, like the other derived fields) and had the controller supply the count via the transient \u2014 mirroring how `namesakeCount` is computed in the controller.\n\n## Test results\n- `./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsPointsAndLevel` passes (owner with email + no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure \u2192 `membershipPoints: 3`, `membershipLevel: 2`).\n\nOne caveat: `./mvnw verify` fails at a JaCoCo `check` gate (lines 0.23 vs. required 0.85, across all ~80 classes). This is **pre-existing and systemic** \u2014 the repo has a single acceptance test covering the whole app, so that bundle-wide gate can't be met by one test and was already failing independent of this change. The test suite itself (`mvn test`) is green.",
