    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered sequence of every validation and side-effect for `POST /api/owners`, as the code stands today. The route is `@RequestMapping(\"/api\")` on `OwnerRestControllerV1` + `/owners` from the generated `OwnersApi` interface, secured to role `OWNER_ADMIN`.\n\n## Access control (before anything else)\n1. **`@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")`** \u2014 non-admins get 403.\n\n## Bean Validation on the request body (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`)\nRuns before the controller method body. Failures \u2192 400 (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`).\n2. `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words via space/'/-)\n3. `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, allows trailing `.`)\n4. `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n5. `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n6. `postcode` \u2014 optional; `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)` when present\n7. `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`\n8. `email` \u2014 optional; `@Size(1..255)`, `@Email` when present\n9. `registrationDate` / `birthDate` \u2014 optional ISO dates\n\n## Controller-body validations & side-effects (in execution order)\n10. **Address normalized** (side-effect): trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST/RD/AVE \u2014 written back onto the DTO.\n11. **`rejectBlankOwnerFields`**: reject whitespace-only firstName/lastName/address/city/telephone \u2192 400.\n12. **`rejectDisposableEmailDomain`**: block mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail domains \u2192 400.\n13. Capture `sharesHousehold` flag.\n14. **`rejectInvalidPostcode`**: if postcode present, must fit the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city \u2192 any 4 digits) \u2192 400.\n15. **`rejectCityAtCapacity`**: \u2265 50 existing owners in that city \u2192 409.\n16. **`rejectFutureRegistrationDate`**: supplied date after today \u2192 400.\n17. **Registration-date defaulting + business-day roll** (side-effect): null \u2192 today; Saturday/Sunday rolled forward to Monday.\n18. **`rejectDailyRegistrationLimit`**: \u2265 100 owners on the resulting registrationDate \u2192 429.\n19. **Telephone normalized** (side-effect + validation): canonicalize to E.164 (assume +61, strip leading 0/non-digits), enforce 8\u201315 digits and per-country length; failure \u2192 400. Written back to DTO.\n20. **Email normalized** (side-effect): lower-cased. Written back to DTO.\n21. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity** (id and pets ignored).\n22. Set derived persisted fields (side-effects): `registrationDate`; **`customerCode`** (`REGION-<8 hex of SHA-256(telephone+lastName)>`); **`namesakeCount`** (count of same first+last); **`householdId`** (SHA-256 of canonical lastName + postcode, null if no postcode).\n23. **`rejectDuplicateIdentity`**: another owner with same `telephone|email|householdId` \u2192 409.\n24. **`rejectHouseholdDuplicate`**: unless `sharesHousehold` true or householdId null, another owner sharing householdId \u2192 409.\n25. Set **`possibleDuplicateOf`** (side-effect): soft-match id (same lastName + postcode, different phone), null if sharesHousehold.\n26. **Persist** (side-effect): `clinicService.saveOwner` \u2192 `@Transactional` insert into `owners`, DB-generated id.\n27. **`householdSize`** computed post-insert (transient, for response only).\n28. **AUDIT log line** emitted (side-effect) \u2014 SLF4J logger `\"AUDIT\"`; the only \"event\" (no ApplicationEventPublisher).\n29. Build response DTO with derived read-only fields (membership number/level/points, locality, ageBand, bulkSignupWarning when >80 same-day, identityKey, possibleDuplicate\u2026), set **`Location: /api/owners/{id}`** header, return **201**.\n\n## Entity-level (Hibernate pre-persist validation, on flush)\n30. `Owner`/`Person` constraints re-checked: firstName/lastName/address/city `@NotEmpty`, postcode `@Pattern`, telephone `@NotEmpty @Pattern(^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$)`, email `@Email`.\n\n## Notable characteristics\n- **No `@Transactional` on `addOwner`** \u2014 every count/duplicate check is its own read transaction, and the save is separate, so all the uniqueness/capacity/limit checks are subject to race conditions (check-then-act, no DB constraint backing them).\n- **No DB uniqueness** (`@Column(unique=...)` absent), no `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@EntityListeners`, no JPA auditing. All uniqueness is enforced in application code only.\n- Several checks (city capacity, namesake count, daily limit, duplicates, household size) each scan all owners via `findAllOwners`.\n\nNote: the endpoint mapping and DTO constraints live under `target/generated-sources/openapi/` (generated from an OpenAPI spec), while the controller logic, validators, service, and entity are in `src/main/java`."
